# The generated x86 problem `max2`, quoted: definitions

`max2M` is `examples/wasm-sim/x86/problems/max2.wat` (a frozen artifact, generated by the
since removed `wasm-sim pcalls --mode problem`) quoted verbatim with `wat3!`: the G simulator's
state API and methods,
local memory, the P-calls translation of the x86-64 function `max2` (`mov rax, rdi; cmp rdi,
rsi; cmovl rax, rsi; ret`) and the SysV wrapper `max2(rdi, rsi) → rax` with
`@ensures (= result (ite (bvsgt rsi rdi) rsi rdi))`.

Functions by index (`0`, `1` are the imports `sys.syscall`, `nd.undef`): `2 off`, `3 load64`,
`4 store64`, `5 rget`, `6 rset`, `7 fget`, `8 fset`, `9 fset6`, `10 mask`, `11 sbit`, `12 u`,
`13 parity`, `14 fres`, `15 rd`, `16 wr`, `17 cond`, `18 alu`, `19 pop`, `20 get`, `21 set`,
`22 i_next`, `23 i_mov_rr`, `24 i_alu_rr`, `25 i_ret`, `26 i_cmov_rr`, `27 f_400005`,
`28 max2`; `max2M.funcs[k]` is function `k + 2`. Globals `0‥15` GPRs, `16` RIP, `17‥23` CF PF AF
ZF SF OF DF.

`Good` is the state invariant the specifications (`Silmaril.Proofs.Sim.X86.Max2`) assume: typed
globals, memory `ma` of type `mt` with a page, and the functions at addresses `0‥28` (the
instance's function `k` at address `k`, as after instantiation into a store holding just the two
host imports). A Silmaril addition.
-/

